# the map
  files lua/scry/map.lua

  Plain text in, structure out, plain text back — byte-identical, so a
  parse/serialize round trip cannot lose anything. Indentation is the
  grammar; a blank line is layout and does not close a claim block.

  contains
    lua/scry/map.lua:parse
    lua/scry/map.lua:serialize
  exercises
    tests/map_spec.lua

# the glass
  files lua/scry/glass.lua

  Two files composed into one editable buffer; :w routes never-blocks to the
  holdout and everything else to the map. state.root is only ever set
  alongside the content it describes — otherwise a second project's beliefs
  save over the first project's map.

  contains
    lua/scry/glass.lua:compose
    lua/scry/glass.lua:split
  exercises
    tests/glass_spec.lua

# exercised claims
  files lua/scry/runs.lua, lua/scry/run.lua

  The dynamic evidence axis. Checking never executes anything; :ScryRun does,
  and records a fingerprint of what it depended on so a pass stops counting as
  one the moment the code moves.

  contains
    lua/scry/runs.lua:stale
    lua/scry/runs.lua:fingerprint
    lua/scry/run.lua:specs
  exercises
    tests/exercises_spec.lua:checking did NOT run the test command
